# Needed Test Cases

## System

- Verify application context starts with default test profile.
- Verify all controllers are reachable through Spring MVC routing.
- Verify global error response shape for validation, not found, conflict, unauthorized, and forbidden errors.
- Verify OpenAPI/Swagger endpoint starts and includes secured endpoints.
- Verify database migrations/schema creation work for test and dev profiles.
- Verify fake external clients are active in dev/test profiles and real clients are not used accidentally.
- Verify endpoint coverage tracking records only controller routes.
- Verify health/basic startup behavior with empty database.

## Auth

- Register user with valid email/password returns JWT and normalized email.
- Register rejects duplicate email case-insensitively.
- Register rejects invalid email, short password, blank fields, and malformed JSON.
- Login returns JWT for valid credentials.
- Login accepts email with different case.
- Login rejects wrong password.
- Login rejects unknown email.
- Current-user endpoint returns authenticated user data.
- Protected endpoints reject missing token.
- Protected endpoints reject malformed token.
- Protected endpoints reject expired/invalid-signature token.
- Auth response never exposes password hash.

## Roles

- `USER` cannot create hackathons.
- `ORGANIZER` can create and manage own hackathons.
- Non-organizer cannot add mentors or judges.
- Organizer cannot assign a user as mentor unless user role is `MENTOR`.
- Organizer cannot assign a user as judge unless user role is `JUDGE`.
- Mentor can view support requests only for assigned hackathons.
- Judge can view/evaluate submissions only for assigned hackathons.
- User cannot view staff-only submission/evaluation/report endpoints.
- Organizer can view registrations, reports, submissions, and evaluations for own hackathon.
- Cross-hackathon staff access is denied.

## Lifecycle

- Hackathon starts in `REGISTRATION_OPEN` after creation.
- Reject invalid date ordering during hackathon creation.
- Allow valid status transition `REGISTRATION_OPEN` -> `IN_PROGRESS`.
- Allow valid status transition `IN_PROGRESS` -> `EVALUATION`.
- Allow valid status transition `EVALUATION` -> `FINISHED`.
- Reject invalid status transitions.
- Reject registration after registration deadline.
- Reject submission before submission phase or after submission deadline.
- Reject evaluation before evaluation phase.
- Reject winner declaration before evaluation phase.
- Reject winner declaration if any submission is unevaluated.
- Reject winner declaration if winner team has no submission.
- Mark hackathon `FINISHED` after declaring winner.
- Prevent declaring winner twice.

## Flow

- Full happy path: register, login, create hackathon, create team, invite member, accept invite, register team, submit, evaluate, declare winner.
- Invite flow rejects non-team-member inviter.
- Invite flow rejects inviting user already on a team.
- Invite flow rejects duplicate invitation.
- Invitee can accept pending invitation.
- Invitee can decline pending invitation.
- Non-invitee cannot accept/decline invitation.
- Accepted/declined invitation cannot be answered again.
- Team registration requires current user to be team member.
- Team registration rejects already registered team.
- Team registration rejects team over max size.
- Submission upsert creates new submission.
- Submission upsert updates existing submission.
- My-team submission endpoint returns current team submission.
- Support request creation requires hackathon in progress and registered team member.
- Mentor call proposal marks support request as call proposed and stores external booking data.
- Rule violation report requires mentor access and registered reported team.
- Organizer can list rule violation reports.
- Payment transaction is created when winner is declared.

## System Tests

- Run full clean automated suite: `GRADLE_USER_HOME=.gradle-home ./gradlew clean test --no-daemon`.
- Run app in dev profile and execute documented manual flow from `TEST.md`.
- Verify seeded dev users can log in with documented credentials.
- Verify seeded demo hackathon appears only when database has no hackathons.
- Verify H2/dev startup can be repeated without duplicate seed data.
- Verify fake payment and calendar clients return deterministic fake IDs/URLs.
- Verify generated test reports contain zero failures and zero errors.
- Verify endpoint coverage threshold task passes.
- Verify unauthorized requests consistently return HTTP 401.
- Verify forbidden role requests consistently return HTTP 403.
- Verify validation failures consistently return HTTP 400 with field details.
